Finger for Retro68

build.sh builds Finger with Retro68 in Docker (the same pinned image as
Mill) and writes build/Finger.bin, a MacBinary file. Copy it to the Mac
and put it in Mill's "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

The code resource is linked flat (-Wl,--mac-flat) with its entry first
(-Wl,-eMILLMAIN), and Finger.r reads it into 'MPlg' 128. The glue
calls RETRO68_RELOCATE, so static data may hold addresses here, but keep
to the SDK's rules so the same source builds with MPW and CodeWarrior.
